From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:21:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 208/342] ffmpeg plugin: encoding on all cores, B_RGB32 to
 YUV420P in NEON

The encoder ran on one thread and swscale converted B_RGB32 to 4:2:0 in
C (71 ms a 1920x1080 frame on the ODROID-C2, half of MPEG-4's cost).
Slice threads on all cores, and the conversion in Advanced SIMD (8 ms,
within 1 of swscale): MPEG-4 at 1920x1080 goes from 6.6 to 27 frames a
second, at 1280x720 from 15 to 61.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
